<title>UNITED NATIONS: U.S., allies, Russia meet on Bosnia.</title>
<headline>U.S., allies, Russia meet on Bosnia.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States, key European allies and Russia met on Thursday to discuss how to shore up peace in Bosnia following this month's elections.</p>
<p>Foreign ministers from the five-nation &quot;contact group&quot; on former Yugoslavia and peace coordinator Carl Bildt met at the U.S. Mission to the United Nations, on the margins of the U.N. General Assembly in New York.</p>
<p>Bildt was due to brief the U.N. Security Council on developments in Bosnia later on Thursday.</p>
<p>The contact group brings together the United States, Russia, France, Germany and Britain.</p>
</text>
